Z||000000||Joe4x4||10-24-2000||01:37 PM||||Been thinking about this....<BR>maybe a 150 shot,<BR>anyone done this , if so what modifaction to the engine would I have to do so as to not destroy the motor .<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-24-2000||01:50 PM||||HEH!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> YEAH! GIVE EM HELL! i had a small shot that made my car pull 13.6 wih no real mods other than fuel. I have however been part of other fogger build-ups. Good forged pistons, and decent rods. the cran to be cryo-realigned and nitrided. and you'll be ok to pull those numbers... with a 150 shot you'll be in the high 11s or low 12s. for the amount of money your gunna spend on rebuilding the motor to with stand the CRAZY shock that nitorus causes you can drop the compression and run 15-18psi and be near the same numbers... Nitrous is sweet and everyone needs it at least once.. but a 150 shot.. uum you migh want a scatter sheild on the fier wall and a bullet proof rear window. not a joke! a dual stage 70 - 100 shot would be ok but get a progressive controller.. they are worth the $500!<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ThatRickGuy||10-24-2000||02:03 PM||||I'm with 1FST2M6 on that one. 150 is a big hit, and a stock 2.8 would blow up with out a lot of work. much better to do a 50-75 or a 70-100. just don't hit the button at idle... bad bad things.||||reg||1
